text	**#91 README: the install command says npm instal**  The README tells the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command fails. The work is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  I have not started the work. The take-in check found signs that the work may already be in progress:  ``` #91: assigned to you #91: label in progress ```  You hold the issue and it has the `in progress` label. The check found no branch for it, so I cannot continue from earlier work. This can mean that another session of yours works on it, on this computer or on another one.  **Is the work running in another session, or should I continue it here?** If it runs somewhere else, I will stop. If I continue here, I will make a worktree on `fix/91-install-command-typo`, fix the typo in `README.md`, run the check and the review, and open the pull request.
